  "claim": "EV-0040 records the CP-0016 host-native parity increment: a standalone gem5 HOSTGPU_NATIVE_CONTROL fixture reusing the existing host protocol, memory, queue, signal, and dispatch state machines; a no-x86/no-production-DSO ELF audit; the source boundary tests; eight legacy VEGA_X86 compatibility regressions; and a self-amdgpu-runtime Triton HSACO metadata probe for two pinned gfx950 images. It proves functional state/memory parity and code-object metadata recognition only. It does not prove PT_LOAD mapping, AQL queue submission, GPU dispatcher/compute-unit execution, Triton end-to-end execution, hardware, timing, or performance, and intentionally contains no final gem5 child HEAD/tree identity.",
